== Q3: shared counter updated by 8 threads x 500000 increments ==

no protection          threads= 8  expected=4000000   actual=2399412    lost=1600588
pthread mutex          threads= 8  expected=4000000   actual=4000000    lost=0
C11 atomic             threads= 8  expected=4000000   actual=4000000    lost=0

The unprotected counter loses updates because counter++ is three
machine instructions (load, add, store) and the scheduler can
interleave two threads between the load and the store.
